P8-spec-001 patch (outside the unit's write_scope: crates/aegis-data-ir is P8-mariadb-001's, crates/aegis-bin is
P8-bin-001's; F4 = crates/aegis-data-ir/src/ir.rs is frozen, so its MANIFEST line is re-frozen in this same patch).
Rationale: SPEC_INVARIANTS §F Phase-8 addendum DENY-M (committed on p8/spec-001) specifies EngineFamily::Mariadb and
its denylist; this is that F4 data change plus the minimum code that keeps the workspace green with it. ir.rs adds the
variant (name "mariadb", ALL now 5), the MARIADB_DENY table (13 keyword items + 5 non-word form entries exported as
MARIADB_FORM_*), and the denylist() arm. lock.rs routes denied_in_sql(Mariadb, ..) to a MariaDB dialect scanner
(backslash/doubled-quote literals, backtick identifiers, '#' and '-- ' comments; refuses '@', ';', '/*!' and '/*M!',
'--' without a following space, unguarded ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE, unterminated text) and gives Mariadb its own upsert
skeleton (ODKU / INSERT..SELECT..FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS, never ON CONFLICT DO, since DO is denied). tests/lock.rs
adds the two unit oracles (each keyword item refused in a fixture lock; each form refused in rendered SQL; the
aegis-adapter-mysql mandated forms pass). aegis-bin plan.rs: its refusals test built "/a//b" and "/a/./b" configs
through parse_config().unwrap(), which now panics because F8 refuses them at load (CFG-5); the case now asserts
NotCanonical at load (the plan's own check is kept). Verified on kamrui with the patch applied over 227f953:
cargo test -p aegis-data-ir --locked (all pass), cargo clippy -p aegis-data-ir --all-targets -D warnings (clean).
Not included (integrator): xtask/src/allowlist.rs (the independent allowlist-lock generator) has FAMILIES without
mariadb, so it refuses a mariadb decl (fail closed); P8-mariadb-001's allowlist.notes-mariadb.lock needs a mariadb
table + skeleton there, and its Deny::hit `_ => resp` fallback should become an explicit arm when that lands.
Apply: git apply units/phase-8/patches/P8-spec-001.patch && python3 -I ci/interfaces.py check

